            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Assign oxidation numbers to all the elements in each of the following species:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "kp2vqkhdkj1ukbf",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "(a) H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "S"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "pw4ub14e572tg42",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "(b) HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2985an22a0b2spo",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "(c) SO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2-"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "vkmgpszqvknueaz",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "Solution"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "vvs36nfewxols89",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(a) H"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "S"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "4orkd2vrzu87bsu",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Hydrogen is combined with sulfur, a nonmental, so the oxidation number for H is +1."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "opybnu0qewg9v5e",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "S is neutral molecule, so the sum of the oxidation numbers for all the atoms in the molecule is 0. The oxidation state of H is +1 and there are 2 hydrogen atoms in this compound, so the total charge due to H is +2. In order to obtain an overall charge of zero for the molecule, the oxidation state for sulfur must be -2."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "v7soi5b2d9ae679",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "tkahx4wh5stdor2",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "a4zed5q6gd21afw",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "(2\\cdot(+1))\\;+\\;(1\\cdot x)\\;=\\;0\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;x\\;=\\;0\\;-\\;2\\;=\\;-2",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(b) HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "nd148a8mg6r2wl2",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Nitrogen and oxygen are nonmetals, so the oxidation number for H -s +1. The oxidation number for each O in this situation, as it is in most, is −2. The overall charge of HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is 0, so the oxidation number for N is determined by:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "x25kezg1r1lw131",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "qviwcoixfstiknf",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "jw8pobop5dg90hi",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "(1\\cdot(+1))\\;+\\;(1\\cdot x)\\;+\\;(3\\cdot(-2))\\;=\\;0\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;x\\;=\\;-1\\;+\\;6\\;=\\;+5",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The oxidation number of N is +5."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ujno784kifpsvwk",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(c) SO"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2−"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3fjef24hnjsvw6l",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The oxidation number for each oxygen in this situation, as it is in most, is −2."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "sxkncp4sexn8lgz",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The overall charge of this polyatomic ion is −2, so the oxidation number for S is determined by:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xei54y6neqps2f3",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "yjxark73o6fuepz",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "n0sjpjkc6clg11w",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "(1\\cdot x)\\;+\\;(4\\cdot(-2))\\;=\\;-2\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;x\\;=\\;-2\\;+\\;8\\;=\\;+6",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The oxidation number of sulfur is +6."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xexohhzdh8iiwui",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
